  "body": "Maintainer decision (question dialog, 2026-11-22): \"Targeted tests, heavy at the cut\"\n\nThis PR changes the process texts to the six points of the decision on #3556 and #2568. It changes no code.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `AGENTS.md`\n  - \"Heavy lanes at review\": a review needs the pinning tests, the touched test binaries (the quick plan), the example catalog suites by name where a post or a toolpath changed, and the light lane. No PR gets the full heavy lanes. A diff that reaches a heavy lane is not \"not ready\" for that reason. No PR is \"owed heavy\". The full heavy lanes run only at the cut, in the cut gate on the cut runner. A `P1` PR under the safety floor gets one targeted heavy step (`cargo xtask gate heavy --only \"<crate> heavy: <target>\"`). `P2` and lower get none. `cargo xtask gate heavy` and `--covers` stay as tools. They are not a condition for \"ready\" or for a merge. The sentence \"the release tier at the cut stays the final check\" stays.\n  - **Owed heavy result** stays as a name, marked as retired, so that its citations resolve.\n  - \"The light lane\": a red light run stays a note on the PR. It does not block the PR by itself. The full heavy steps of the red twins run at the cut, in the cut gate. A local run never replaces the cut gate.\n  - The quick pass and \"When PRs merge\": a heavy lane result is not a condition, except the targeted step of a `P1` PR under the safety floor.\n- `.claude/skills/gate/SKILL.md`: the heavy tier row, the heavy lane text, a new \"targeted heavy step\" item, the wave form as an optional tool, the owed rule marked as retired.\n- `.claude/skills/work-issue/SKILL.md`: the worker names the review tests in the PR body. Only a `P1` PR under the safety floor runs the targeted heavy step.\n- `.claude/skills/review-prs/SKILL.md`: step 2e is now \"Targeted tests at review\".\n- `.claude/skills/merge-ready/SKILL.md`: step 4a is optional. The command and the `<!-- heavy-wave: ... -->` comment format stay. No merge waits for a record. Item 11 keeps one heavy condition: the targeted step of a `P1` PR under the safety floor.\n- `.claude/agents/PR-reviewer.md`: step 5 runs the example catalog tests, the light lane, and the targeted heavy step for a `P1` PR under the safety floor only. The review comment lists those steps. \"Not run\" is never a pass for a required step.\n- `docs/decisions/3556-targeted-tests-at-review.md`: the decision entry.\n\nNo change: `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION`, `xtask/`, workflows, the known-fail marker rules, the cut rules, the pixel snapshot rules. `coordinator.md`, `issue-worker-*.md`, `gate-runner.md` and the `classify-effort` skill have no text that demands heavy lanes, so they do not change.\n\n## Follow-up `c2dd094e9`\n\n- The full heavy lanes run at the cut, in the cut gate on the cut runner, in all the process files. The earlier text named the post-merge runner. `.github/workflows/post-merge.yml` runs only the batch tier (`cargo xtask gate batch`), and the batch tier has no release heavy lanes. The decision file records that the maintainer's words named the post-merge runner, and why the text now names the cut gate.\n- The light-lane rule drops the local rerun clause. The full heavy steps of the red twins run in the cut gate. They do not run locally before the cut.\n- The xtask pin is renamed to `review_requires_targeted_heavy_tests_on_both_paths`. It pins the runner routing into step 5 for a `P1` targeted step. The `3460` decision cites the new name.\n\n## Gate\n\nRun on head `c2dd094e9`, with `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=3`:\n\n- `cargo test -p xtask --bin xtask heavy_plan_tests`: 11 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo test -p xtask --bin xtask light_tests`: 6 passed, 0 failed.\n- `#[test]` count in `xtask/src/heavy_plan_tests.rs`: 11.\n- Red on reverse: the routing pin fails when the runner-to-step-5 line is removed. The retired-demand pin fails when `report \"heavy lanes not run\" as a blocker` returns.\n\nThe quick plan selects `xtask unit tests` for this diff. The diff reaches no heavy lane.\n\n## Open\n\n1. Closed by `38eae631e`: the two xtask unit tests follow the new law. The renamed test `review_requires_targeted_heavy_tests_on_both_paths` pins the new law and the runner routing into step 5. The `#[test]` count stays 11.\n2. \"The touched test binaries (the quick plan)\" when the quick plan falls back to the whole batch plan (a change in geometry, cl or a `Cargo.toml`): this PR does not decide it. See #3557.\n3. Answered. The maintainer's comment on #3556 (2026-11-22, 19:37) says the full heavy steps of the red twins do not run locally before the cut. They run in the cut gate. `AGENTS.md` and the decision file now say this.\n4. The targeted heavy step selects one heavy binary (`--only \"<crate> heavy: <target>\"`), not single test functions. The gate skill gives no form that runs one ignored test by name in release.\n5. The heavy lock (decision point 5) is not in any process file. It is a local rule, so this PR adds no text for it.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: medium\n\nRefs #2568\nRefs #3557\nFixes #3556\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
